EXPLANATION = {"title": "Chain Integrity", "principle": "Sequential C-alpha atoms stay within 4.5 Angstrom of each other.", "rationale": "The pinned code (definition v2, WP-SCI-1) measures the maximum CA(i)-CA(i+1) distance for IMMEDIATELY sequential same-chain residues only (adjacent residue numbers, insertion codes honored, chains never joined); ideal ~3.8 A. A missing residue span (numbering gap) is skipped as absent density, not treated as a chain break; a genuine coordinate discontinuity between adjacent-numbered residues still vetoes above 4.5 A."}
